# ship:begin (owned by ship init; repo-specific lines go below the end marker)
# Allowlist: the images build from the dirs below only. A new root-level file stays out of the context without anyone
# having to remember this list. BuildKit reads the -f Containerfile outside these rules.
*
!backend
!ui
# The host's node_modules (darwin native binaries) would land on top of the image's own install; the image builds
# dist itself.
ui/node_modules
ui/dist
ui/coverage
# ship:end

# The node stage always produces dist/. A local `make fe-build` leaves hashed
# index-*.js chunks here, and COPY backend/ would carry them into the image,
# where the stage's output merges on top instead of replacing them -- so stale
# chunks shipped inside go:embed. Excluded, the image holds only what the
# stage built.
backend/internal/hub/web/dist/
